{
  "description": "Forecasts of Sweden's municipal tax base (per cent change a year) as SKR's December circulars compare them, table 'De senaste skatteunderlagsprognoserna'. Read from the circulars' PDFs on 2026-11-25; the ESV rows were recomputed from ESV's own Prognostabeller (Beskattningsbar förvärvsinkomst) and agree to the decimal, except 2025 in the November 2021 forecast (circular 3.7, workbook 3.6).",
  "notes": [
    "The government's rows are budget propositions. For the current and the next year they are the fixed uppräkningsfaktorer (for example 1,020 and 1,022 in the budget for 2021), set in September.",
    "The forecasts are not from the same day: the government's is up to three months older than SKR's, ESV's zero to three.",
    "The government's rows are read from SKR's table, not from the budget propositions themselves.",
    "Konjunkturinstitutet publishes no forecast of the municipal tax base in Konjunkturläget, only the wage sum (Tabell A7, Lönesumma, justerad för utland) and the municipal sector's tax revenue (Tabell A23). The wage sum is another quantity and is recorded apart, not compared."
